{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024663-hurt-locker-violent-skills-and-academics-problem","id":1024663,"title":"[Hurt Locker] Violent Skills and Academics problem","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-31T01:11:28-08:00","id":1024663,"title":"[Hurt Locker] Violent Skills and Academics problem","content":"So I very like almost all Violent Skills usage shown in sourcebook. I have only one big beef with shown rules \u2013 Academics Skill usage. First off, whole \u2018you can make of character lose his job or position\u2019 sounds much more as Politics actions in first place. But even if we agree that Academics can made you \u2018look worse\u2019 in researches or education circles, it still should be rather limited to Mental Merits only. Because, can writing paper overthrow your enemies academic thesis can really stop him from being Barfly? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Or that Academics writing can make salesman lose his job? \u2018My research points that whales are 3 tones heavier than product you sell!\u2019 \u2018Joe, you lose job, because this client made scientific paper on our main product. Even if you are not responsible for it\u2019s creation.\u2019 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Side note: Not to mention that Resources are <b>not</b> your earnings from job but stashed money that is unrelated to you being haired or not. ) Most I can see in Social Merits area of this \u2018bad mouthing\u2019 is lose of 1 Status dot in particular circles \u2013 as Academics related endeavors are rarely connected as much to you real positions in your organizations. It\u2019s much more \u2018Joe, we have a problem on bad scientific press on you\u2019 than \u2018Joe, you are fired, because of whole whale thing!\u2019<br /> <br /> So the topic question is simple \u2013 <b>What other action can be used as \u2018violent\u2019 use of Academics?</b> Because, as it is written, I can at most see it usable to make you lose your Mental Merits by \u2018researchers battles\u2019 in journals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T03:50:25-08:00","id":1024698,"title":"","content":"I assume the default use is less about &quot;writing bad reviews&quot; and more about being Batman, where you research the target in organized, efficient manner, then identify what is the most optimal way to deny them target resource, and putting that plan in motion. It can be bad mouthing, it can be something else; academics here seems to represent your ability to conduct disciplined mental work and research, and then using fruits of it.<br /> <br /> Like, you are not badmouthing someone's storehouse away, you find out that leader of a local gang got rejected at that spot and hates it to the point where you can see a way to make them go trash it for you.<br /> Or, if you are using the instant-quick-version, GM might say &quot;sure, you figured out that the best way to destroy it is to burn it down, and you think that you can grab the materials here and there...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 12-31-2016, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:33:34-08:00","id":1024709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024663-hurt-locker-violent-skills-and-academics-problem?p=1024698#post1024698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume the default use is less about &quot;writing bad reviews&quot; and more about being Batman, where you research the target in organized, efficient manner, then identify what is the most optimal way to deny them target resource, and putting that plan in motion. It can be bad mouthing, it can be something else; academics here seems to represent your ability to conduct disciplined mental work and research, and then using fruits of it.<br /> <br /> Like, you are not badmouthing someone's storehouse away, you find out that leader of a local gang got rejected at that spot and hates it to the point where you can see a way to make them go trash it for you.<br /> Or, if you are using the instant-quick-version, GM might say &quot;sure, you figured out that the best way to destroy it is to burn it down, and you think that you can grab the materials here and there...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That reads a lot like Investigation, though. What does the actua entry for Investigation in Violent Skills say?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:40:26-08:00","id":1024711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024663-hurt-locker-violent-skills-and-academics-problem?p=1024709#post1024709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reads a lot like Investigation, though. What does the actua entry for Investigation in Violent Skills say?</div> </div> </div> </div>Investigation can show you weak spots in combat with opponent. It's just look like 'Sherlock boxing'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2_vbmZJBXSA\" data-code=\"2_vbmZJBXSA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2_vbmZJBXSA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:58:42-08:00","id":1024715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024663-hurt-locker-violent-skills-and-academics-problem?p=1024711#post1024711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Investigation can show you weak spots in combat with opponent. It's just look like 'Sherlock boxing'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2_vbmZJBXSA\" data-code=\"2_vbmZJBXSA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2_vbmZJBXSA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. So that's how Batman does his stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T05:07:37-08:00","id":1024716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024663-hurt-locker-violent-skills-and-academics-problem?p=1024709#post1024709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reads a lot like Investigation, though. What does the actua entry for Investigation in Violent Skills say?</div> </div> </div> </div>My initial reaction was similar. Remember though that these mechanics aren't married to their skills, so using Academics mechanic with Streetwise, Politics and Investigation seems to feel very natural. On the other hand, Investigation specific ability is unique enough that I can't see it being used by anything else than Investigation and fighting skills themselves.<br /> Actually, you probably easily give them a make up change and use them for Intimidation and Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> The biggest difference you probably would have to make would be changing Investigation's &quot;finding a hole&quot; into &quot;creating a hole&quot; using other skills; something like &quot;if you Intimidated the target in past scenes, [rest of Watch and Learn mechanics]&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T05:10:42-08:00","id":1024718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1024663-hurt-locker-violent-skills-and-academics-problem?p=1024716#post1024716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My initial reaction was similar. Remember though that these mechanics aren't married to their skills, so using Academics mechanic with Streetwise, Politics and Investigation seems to feel very natural. On the other hand, Investigation specific ability is unique enough that I can't see it being used by anything else than Investigation and fighting skills themselves.<br /> Actually, you probably easily give them a make up change and use them for Intimidation and Subterfuge.<br /> <br /> EDIT<br /> The biggest difference you probably would have to make would be changing Investigation's &quot;finding a hole&quot; into &quot;creating a hole&quot; using other skills; something like &quot;if you Intimidated the target in past scenes, [rest of Watch and Learn mechanics]&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the purpose of the whole Violent Skills section seem to be about broadening the players' perspectives on Skills, by introducing unexpected but totally legit cases of using those Skills in the one thing CofD games is sure to have plenty of. In which case I believe we have enough leeway to do different things with different Skills.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}